## Reagents

wg-reagent-name-coca-alkaloid = coca alkaloid
wg-reagent-desc-coca-alkaloid = A bitter green extract ground from coca leaves. Chemists cook it into cocaine.
wg-reagent-name-cocaine = cocaine
wg-reagent-desc-cocaine = A white stimulant powder. Short, bright and talkative, with a flat come-down.
wg-reagent-name-crack = crack
wg-reagent-desc-crack = Cocaine cooked into a smokable base. Hits harder, ends sooner and pulls back hard.
wg-reagent-name-opium = opium
wg-reagent-desc-opium = The sticky brown sap of the opium poppy. Chilled, a splash of water sets it into resin. A slow, warm downer.
wg-reagent-name-heroin = heroin
wg-reagent-desc-heroin = A refined opioid powder. Kills pain, slows breathing, and Naloxone reverses it.
wg-reagent-name-redline-base = redline base
wg-reagent-desc-redline-base = A dark, oily intermediate. Useless until it's finished.
wg-reagent-name-redline = Redline
wg-reagent-desc-redline = A combat stimulant that shrugs off stuns and pain while it burns the heart. When it ends, so do you.
wg-reagent-name-anvil-base = anvil base
wg-reagent-desc-anvil-base = A grey, metallic intermediate. Useless until it's finished.
wg-reagent-name-anvil = Anvil
wg-reagent-desc-anvil = A combat drug that lets blows land soft. Every hit it holds off comes back later.
wg-reagent-name-lattice-residue = Lattice residue
wg-reagent-desc-lattice-residue = Ground exotic matter. It hums faintly, and it isn't safe to drink.
wg-reagent-name-chorus-base = chorus base
wg-reagent-desc-chorus-base = A shimmering violet intermediate. Useless until it's finished.
wg-reagent-name-chorus = Chorus
wg-reagent-desc-chorus = A psychedelic cut with the Lattice. Users hear things out there, and sometimes see them.
wg-reagent-name-halo-base = halo base
wg-reagent-desc-halo-base = A sweet golden intermediate. Useless until it's finished.
wg-reagent-name-halo = Halo
wg-reagent-desc-halo = An empathogen that makes everyone nearby feel like old friends. Runs hot.

